    <section class="section" id="exhibit-list">
    <h2><span class="num">02 — What Happened</span>The Exhibit List</h2>

    <p>Florida Attorney General James Uthmeier filed the underlying complaint against OpenAI on June 1, 2026, alleging violations of the Florida Deceptive and Unfair Trade Practices Act (FDUTPA), negligence, gross negligence, defective design, failure to warn, fraudulent misrepresentation, and public nuisance. OpenAI removed the case to federal court on July 2, arguing that a Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) count created federal jurisdiction. On September 8, U.S. District Judge Aileen M. Cannon granted Florida's motion to remand, ruling that defendants "clearly fail[ed] to satisfy the requirements" for federal jurisdiction. The court was "entirely unconvinced" of OpenAI's arguments. The case returned to Highlands County.</p>

